    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d145">

                <pb facs="0193" n="183" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93/543: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-22T00:00:00-04:00">December 22,
                            1943—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1845. There is being transmitted by separate telegram<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d145-f1"/> a summary of <hi rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi>
                    article by Nathaniel Peffer, referred to in your 2422 of December 15, and full
                    text is being forwarded by air pouch.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d145-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Peffer’s article is restrained in tone and is in fact a plea for a balanced view
                    and for the exercise of forbearance in discussions of American-Chinese
                    relations. In achieving this balance the author has spoken frankly, but the
                    Department does not consider that the article is unfair to China or overdrawn,
                    although certain passages, especially the references to Madame Chiang, are
                    perhaps not in the best of taste.</p>
                <p>Department will endeavor to supply the Embassy by telegraph with summaries of
                    articles published in the United States containing criticism of China deemed to
                    have a controversial character. OWI states that copies of Peffer and other
                    critical articles had already been sent by air mail to Fisher, who will
                    doubtless be willing to make similar material available to you in future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
